UPDATE "evidence_population_match" SET "match_grade" = 'PARTIAL', "mismatch_note" = 'EXACT on the population served (people who use wheelchairs and scooters). Two limits are written so the grade is not read as representativeness: the report says the sample is not proportional to national estimates of device type (powered chairs oversampled), and the turning tasks were done in a built mock-up, so a person using a wheelchair in a real corridor with a companion or a door swing is outside it. Scooter users are in the sample and are a different device class from wheelchairs; the report separates them in its tables. || REGRADED 2026-11-06 by session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2: EXACT -> PARTIAL. Adversarial pass: MOB is defined as general mobility limitation including walking, balance, or wheeled mobility; the 495 are wheeled mobility device users only (PDF page 17) and no ambulant person with a mobility limitation is in the sample. For parameter 4 (corridor width, which serves people with walking aids too) EXACT overstated. Also: the report says data were collected at three sites (PDF page 18); the study_population wording ''recruited in'' is the batch''s.' WHERE "match_id" = 'session_2026-11-06-pipel-REF-00468-MOB';

-- search_executions: 0 insert(s), 3 update(s)
UPDATE "search_executions" SET "findings_note" = 'No Co-1 source. Fifteen results: UK housing-association and local-authority wheelchair housing design guides (HousingLIN, Camden, Southwark), a Scottish government consultation, Massachusetts 521 CMR 6, a Texas TAS page, a South African SANS 10400 page, an ADA figures page and a Wiley excerpt. They state 1500 mm turning space, 840 to 900 mm door clear opening and 1200 mm hallways, all from code or planning-guidance bodies, none from a disabled persons organisation. R14: a WELL-FORMED query for the question asked; the long natural-language shape returned code pages, so the zero Co-1 yield is a wrong-index and a query-shape result together, not proof of absence. A targeted DPO search (Disability Rights UK, Scope, Centre for Accessible Environments) is not done by this batch and stays open. Results listed in the transcript only (WebSearch leaves no payload); the I5 ledger holds the query. || CORRECTED 2026-11-06: The result list held 17 links, not 15 (results_found cannot be amended): the two omitted above are an Illinois JCAR administrative-code .docx and a yamol.tw exam-essay page. Door clear opening figures in the results: 840 mm (UK housing guide, ideally 900), 800 mm (Scottish consultation), 900 mm with 840 mm where unavoidable (Camden).', "updated_at" = '2026-11-06 04:56' WHERE "exec_id" = 201;
UPDATE "search_executions" SET "findings_note" = 'No systematic review of manoeuvring space. Ten results: the Steinfeld 2010 review (informahealthcare, DOI 10.1080/10400430903520280, already candidate 151), a Stanford RESNA 2010 worksheet, five pages of the Anthropometry of Wheeled Mobility Project Final Report transcribed on corada.com, ISO 7176-5 (a measurement standard), a CORE PDF (403 on retrieval) and a 2019 International Journal of Occupational Safety and Ergonomics paper on wheelchair-user anthropometry (a systematic review of body and device size, not of space requirements). The surprise is the report: a primary measurement study of 495 wheeled mobility users, found through its transcription, and followed at the next search. The prior (nothing new) was wrong. || CORRECTED 2026-11-06: The journal of the 2019 paper (DOI 10.1080/10803548.2019.1567974) is not stated in the search result; the name given above was inferred from the DOI prefix and is withdrawn. || CORRECTED 2026-11-06: Of the five corada.com pages in the result list, four are pages of the Anthropometry of Wheeled Mobility Project Final Report and one (4-5-maneuvering-clearances) belongs to a different corada document, Standards and anthropometry for WhM. Three payloads of this search''s hits are persisted (da321ad57f7fc3f5.html, 41510aa497941b7d.html, 0b55e83d8e9ee3d4.html, the last a 403 page) but cannot be linked as result artefacts: the writer requires the query text to name the payload host.', "updated_at" = '2026-11-06 04:56' WHERE "exec_id" = 202;
UPDATE "search_executions" SET "findings_note" = 'Lookup of a source surfaced by exec 202. The first result is the PDF on idea.ap.buffalo.edu; the others are corada.com transcriptions of its sections, an Access Board page on wheelchair seat height, and a humancentereddesign.org library entry. Retrieved 2026-11-06 (HTTP 200, 14,986,049 bytes, 173 pages, sha256 e664fb2f8174f4f8) and admitted as REF-00468, the stash id that already held this title (the stash row carries an unrelated Husbanken URL: the GAP-008 shuffled-field defect). The corada transcription pages (da321ad57f7fc3f5.html, 41510aa497941b7d.html) were retrieved first and are not the source of any row. || CORRECTED 2026-11-06: Harm flag raised after the adversarial pass. The admitted report states that fewer than half of its manual and powered wheelchair users completed a 360-degree turn within the US standard turning diameter, and that none of its scooter users did (PDF page 65), and that the 1525 mm 180-degree standard accommodates fewer than half of its scooter users (PDF page 62). Extraction 183 (ADA 1525 mm) and extraction 193 keep contested = 0: no writer amends that column. The IDeA ''What is Anthropometry?'' page (idea.ap.buffalo.edu/?p=157) was also in the result list and was not opened. The query_text carries a ''|| retrieved <url>'' suffix because the artefact link requires the host and path in it.', "harm_finding" = 1, "updated_at" = '2026-11-06 04:56' WHERE "exec_id" = 203;

-- source_scans: 4 insert(s), 0 update(s)
INSERT INTO "source_scans" ("scan_id", "ref_id", "mode", "catalogue_version", "target_parameter_id", "text_scope", "pages_read", "pages_total", "file_sha256", "open_pass_done", "method", "notes", "created_at", "created_by_session", "updated_at", "updated_by_session") VALUES (15, 'REF-00468', 'catalogue', 12, NULL, 'full', 173, 173, 'bae3334434e4025dbc3e17311e4ecb28626f986f3a0eaceebc180e39a1072da8', 0, 'pre-screen', 'Second reading after the adversarial pass; where it differs it replaces the first scan of this source. CORRECTIONS. (1) The first note said the report states no door clear width and no force a door or control may require. That is false: section 4.3.8 (PDF pages 112-113) recommends 2 lbf (9 N) for pinch-grip controls and keeping 5 lbf (22.2 N) for power-grip controls and for opening doors, and section 4.3.9 (PDF page 114) says a clear opening of 860 mm would accommodate the widest occupied devices; these are now filed under parameters 6 and 9. The first scan stopped its keyword reading at pages 34, 48, 67, 90 and 92; door occurs on 29 pages and force on 20. (2) The first note said zero hits for overhead or vertical clearance; overhead occurs on PDF page 35 and head clearance on PDF page 23, in neither case as a clearance value for a route; headroom has no hit. (3) The first note said pages 16-17 were read in full for sampling: PDF page 16 is a header page; the sampling and recruitment text is on pages 17-18 (the 351, 100 and 44 are on page 18). (4) The pages_read figure of the scan row counts the pages held, not the pages read; the pages read in full are about 20 (17-18, 61-66, 97-101, 112-114). (5) The bibliography begins at PDF page 170 (report page 159), not 159. Sentence-form figures only are filed; tables are cell sequences without row labels. Still not read end to end.', '2026-11-06 04:56', 'session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2', '2026-11-06 04:56', 'session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2');
INSERT INTO "source_scans" ("scan_id", "ref_id", "mode", "catalogue_version", "target_parameter_id", "text_scope", "pages_read", "pages_total", "file_sha256", "open_pass_done", "method", "notes", "created_at", "created_by_session", "updated_at", "updated_by_session") VALUES (16, 'REF-01028', 'catalogue', 12, NULL, 'full', NULL, NULL, 'b9353457a95a925b4b646e2c0263d35bdc1b973964f28645110569d14717047a', 0, 'pre-screen', 'Second reading after the adversarial pass; where it differs it replaces the first scan of this source. CORRECTIONS. The first screen keyed on anchura libre and missed two spellings: lift doors in art 16.3 (ancho de paso libre minimo de 90 cm, now filed under parameter 9) and ramp sections in art 14.2.a (anchura minima libre de paso de 1,80 m, now filed under parameter 4). The first note named two articles with a 1,50 m circle (8, 27); the phrase circulo de 1,50 m occurs seven times in at least five articles (play areas, lift cabins, tables, kiosk approach zones, drinking fountains and the two filed in art 34); the others are not filed.', '2026-11-06 04:56', 'session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2', '2026-11-06 04:56', 'session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2');
INSERT INTO "source_scans" ("scan_id", "ref_id", "mode", "catalogue_version", "target_parameter_id", "text_scope", "pages_read", "pages_total", "file_sha256", "open_pass_done", "method", "notes", "created_at", "created_by_session", "updated_at", "updated_by_session") VALUES (17, 'REF-01031', 'catalogue', 12, NULL, 'full', 22, 22, 'e61147623cbd9d61ea5ff3e25e97c24b00a4d8314d9414c49120c87e967adc42', 0, 'pre-screen', 'Third reading, same day; where it differs it replaces the first and second scans. CORRECTIONS. (1) The first note said items 6, 7 and the toilet clauses were read in full and listed what was stated and not filed; it missed, now filed: item 1(마)(2) tree pruning to 2.1 m (parameter 11), item 13(나)(1)(다) stall door 0.9 m (parameter 9) and item 12(가)(1) ramp width 1.2 m (parameter 4). Stated and still not filed: item 9 lift-front space of 1.4 m by 1.4 m (a lift-front space, not stated as a turning space); the 0.9 m relaxation of the ramp width. (2) Extraction 211 cites item 8(나)(1)(가); the clause is item 13(나)(1)(가) (item 8 is the stairs item); the correction is on the row. (3) pages_read counts the pages held (22), not pages read in full.', '2026-11-06 04:56', 'session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2', '2026-11-06 04:56', 'session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2');
INSERT INTO "source_scans" ("scan_id", "ref_id", "mode", "catalogue_version", "target_parameter_id", "text_scope", "pages_read", "pages_total", "file_sha256", "open_pass_done", "method", "notes", "created_at", "created_by_session", "updated_at", "updated_by_session") VALUES (18, 'REF-01032', 'catalogue', 12, NULL, 'partial', 5, 20, 'de24554e5ad496f16ff1c0f94a1f6ec0b477b3f9948626dac38d0ed054e06933', 0, 'pre-screen', 'Second reading after the adversarial pass; where it differs it replaces the first scan of this source. CORRECTION. The first note said parameters 6, 7, 8, 10, 11 are not on the pages held and were not examined. Page 20 of 20 (held) carries item 4.12.1(4), controls and operable elements to be operable without a force above 22 N: now filed under parameter 6. Page 10 carries item 2.5.4 (ramp width not below 1,2 m: now filed under parameter 4) and item 2.6.4(2) (lift door clear width not below 0,8 m: stated, not filed). Parameters 7, 8, 10, 11 remain not examined: most of the decree is not in the held text.', '2026-11-06 04:56', 'session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2', '2026-11-06 04:56', 'session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2');

